2)Self hosted integration Run time -  whenever our data is available in diffrent space
Ex- (source data - SQL DB  and sink data - Cloud DB)


D)Azure storage account contains 4 types of storage services -
1) Blob Storage- when we have unstructured data like video, audio, test file
2) File Storage- To store file on shared path, where all team members can acess file.
3) Table storage -when we have structured data.Data is stored in Tabular form
4) Queue Storage - File transfers one after one (After transfer of 1 file it goes to next file)

E)Azure account contains 3 types-
1)Blob storage -  when we have unstructured data
2)General Purpose V1 account- 
3)General Purpose V2 account -Latest vesion of Azure

F)Acess Tier we have 3 types -
1)Hot Tier- when we have to acess data Frequently
2)Cold Tier- when we don't have to acess data Frequently
3)Archive -when we have to acess data Rarely

G)Trigger- Trigger are objects that enable automatic execution of pipeline based on predefined or schedules.
 a)Schedule Trigger - The event triggered at a scheduled time (min,hour,second)
	b)Tumbling Trigger - The event is triggered in past and future time
	c)Event storage Trigger - When we upload or delete a file other than a Txt file to run a pipeeline then this Event is triggered.
 d)Manual Triger- Allows manual execution of pipeline by a user or external System.

H)GetMedaData Activity-GetMetadata retrieves metadata about files or datasets
1)ItemNam- Name of the file or folder
2)ItemType - Type of the file or folder.Returned value is file or folder
3)size- Size of the file in bytes.Applicable only to files.
4)Createddatetime - created datetime of the file or folder
5)LastModified - LastModified datetime of the file or folder
6)Childitems- List of sub folders and diles in a given folder.Applicable only to folders.Returned value is a list of a name and type of each child item.
7)Structure- Data structure of a file or relational DB table.Returned value is a list of a  column name and column type
8)ColumnCount- Noumber of columns in a file or  relational table
9)Exists-When a file, folder or table exists.

